| Command                                                           | Purpose                  | What Happens                                                                                                                            |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `git config --global user.name "Randev"`                          | Set your Git username    | Git saves "Randev" as the author name for future commits on this computer.                                                              |
| `git config --global user.email "itsgeekguard@gmail.com"`         | Set your Git email       | Git saves this email and associates future commits with it. GitHub uses it to link commits to your account.                             |
| `git add .`                                                       | Stage changes            | Git scans the current folder and places all new, modified, and deleted files into the staging area, preparing them for the next commit. |
| `git commit -m "Week 1: First Debian VM created with SSH access"` | Create a commit          | Git creates a permanent snapshot of all staged files and records the message, author, timestamp, and commit ID in the local repository. |
| `git push`                                                        | Upload commits to GitHub | Git sends any local commits that are not yet on GitHub to the remote repository.                                                        |
